            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of chronic hand eczema with oral 9-cis-retinoic acid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">9-cis-Retinoic acid (9-cis-RA) has a particular pattern of binding and activating retinoid receptors. Treatment of chronic hand eczema is often refractory to conventional treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Evaluation of oral 9-cis-RA therapy in chronic hand eczema in a pilot study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Thirty-eight patients with refractory chronic hand eczema were treated in an exploratory open-label study with oral 9-cis-RA.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Twenty-one (55%) showed a very good response, 13 (34%) a good response, 2 (5.5%) a moderate response and 2 (5.5%) no response. Side effects were mild.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">9-cis-RA is a valuable drug when given at low doses to patients with chronic hand eczema.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright (R) 2000 S. Karger AG, Basel</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
